From: cod3 port
Subject: [PATCH] ui: HDR10 output (BT.2020, PQ) with a subtle highlight boost

New settings (src/ui/presenter.cpp): display_hdr (off by default),
display_hdr_paper_white (nits for SDR white, 80-500, 203) and
display_hdr_peak (nits for the brightest highlight, 100-10000, 600).

With display_hdr on, the Vulkan presenter asks for an HDR10 swapchain
(VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace: VK_COLOR_SPACE_HDR10_ST2084_EXT with a 10-bit
format). If the surface offers one (the display and the desktop are in HDR
mode), the picture is painted as before into an SDR canvas
(R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT, as big as the swapchain), then a last pass
(shaders/hdr10_encode_ps.frag) turns it into HDR10: 2.2 decode, BT.709 to
BT.2020 primaries, highlights above 80% of SDR white eased up to
display_hdr_peak on luminance (hues keep), SDR white at
display_hdr_paper_white, PQ encode. The canvas's alpha is the UI's coverage
(cleared to 0; the guest output writes RGB only; the UI drawers add alpha),
so the UI stays at paper white. VK_EXT_hdr_metadata, if present, gets the
mastering metadata. Turning display_hdr on or off reconnects the presenter
(the swapchain is made again). Otherwise the window gets SDR as before, and
the log says why once; so it does if a step only HDR10 needs fails (an
HDR10 swapchain the driver refuses is made again in SDR; after a failed
canvas, SDR until display_hdr is turned off and on).
Only 10-bit formats the device can draw into are used.
rex/ui/hdr_output.h tells the app what the window gets. The Direct3D 12 presenter has no HDR10 output (state kNotSupported).

Must apply before 0046 (vulkan_presenter.cpp).
---
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/hdr_output.h b/include/rex/ui/hdr_output.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..90afd16
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/rex/ui/hdr_output.h
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+/**
+ * HDR10 output: what the window gets (settings display_hdr,
+ * display_hdr_paper_white, display_hdr_peak in src/ui/presenter.cpp).
+ *
+ * With display_hdr on, the Vulkan presenter asks the window system for an
+ * HDR10 swapchain (VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace: VK_COLOR_SPACE_HDR10_ST2084_EXT,
+ * 10-bit). If it gets one, the picture is painted as before into an SDR canvas
+ * and a last pass turns that into HDR10 (BT.2020 primaries, PQ brightness):
+ * the picture keeps its SDR look at display_hdr_paper_white nits and only its
+ * brightest highlights go up to display_hdr_peak; the UI stays at paper white.
+ * Otherwise the window gets SDR as before. The Direct3D 12 presenter has no
+ * HDR10 output.
+ */
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace rex::ui {
+
+enum class HdrOutput : int32_t {
+  // display_hdr is off (or no window yet).
+  kOff = 0,
+  // The window gets HDR10 (BT.2020, SMPTE ST 2084).
+  kActive = 1,
+  // display_hdr is on, but the display / desktop offers no HDR10 format to
+  // this window (HDR off in the system's display settings, a display without
+  // HDR, or a Vulkan driver without VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace).
+  kNotOffered = 2,
+  // display_hdr is on, but the graphics API in use has no HDR10 output
+  // (Direct3D 12).
+  kNotSupported = 3,
+};
+
+// What the window gets now. Any thread.
+HdrOutput GetHdrOutput();
+// For the presenters.
+void SetHdrOutput(HdrOutput state);
+
+}  // namespace rex::ui
